            "review_text": "adrian m\nLos Angeles, California43 contributions\n0\nOkay salad but beware\nApr 2019\nThis was really close to my hotel and saw locals eating here the night before so tried it out for lunch the next day. I had the dried beef salad which had 3 different kinds of meat over shredded green papaya and herbs with a light dressing. Overall, the salad was okay. One of the meats was an organ meat (not sure which) and that was not my cup of tea.\n\nWhat was weird was there are no prices on the menu, which should have been a red flag. When I asked to pay, the person told me 55K VND and when I looked confused and asked another person, he said 35K. Honestly, I don’t know if that is even the real price. With so many options to eat, avoid this one and go somewhere else. The food was not good enough to feel like you’ve been ripped off.\nRead more\nWritten April 26, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
